      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "content": "Function-like Macros"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "We can also use the #define preprocessor to create macros that work like a function. For example,"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "content": "#define circle_area(r) (3.1415 * r * r)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Let's take a working example:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "content": "1#include <iostream>\n2\n3#define PI 3.1415\n4#define circle_area(r) (PI * r * r)\n5\n6using namespace std;\n7\n8int main() {\n9\n10    double radius = 2.5;\n11    \n12\n13    // call the function-like macro\n14    // pass radius as argument\n15    double area = circle_area(radius);\n16\n17    \n18    cout << \"Area = \" << area;  // 19.6344\n19\n20    return 0;\n21}"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Output"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "text",
      "content": "Area = 19.6344"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Here, the code circle_area(radius) expands to:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "content": "3.1415 * 2.5 * 25"
    },
